      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with the principle, but not in this form for a few reasons including: sync flags aren\u0027t part of the cache key, --output-json is skipped on cache hit, gclient sync no longer repairs a broken checkout, etc.\n\nI remember there was a previous \"no sync\" effort that tried to do the same thing, but skips per-dep fetches and runs the full sync pipeline. see https://crbug.com/40230011 and https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/tools/depot_tools/+/main:gclient.py;l\u003d2306-2360;drc\u003df394ab2c993283e94680ca13db98b99927868e98 \n\nI\u0027d recommend building on top of that rather than adding a parallel mechanism and keep it opt-in",
      "parentUuid": "0b037625_fbdc1c0a",
      "revId": "a1f49d4569e956d95704e0252950cb12e3634367",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
